  "security_implications": "The chunk hardwires msg_fifo_rdata to all-ones and msg_fifo_rerror to all-ones, preventing any read from that port, which may prevent exposure of sensitive internal state. The hmac_err interrupt instance latches err_valid and can escalate HMAC errors (possibly security violations) to the system. The interrupt control itself is standard and relies on CSR access control, but the error signal's semantic is security-relevant.",
